<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0008150> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A biological process is the execution of a genetically-encoded biological module or program. It consists of all the steps required to achieve the specific biological objective of the module. A biological process is accomplished by a particular set of molecular functions carried out by specific gene products (or macromolecular complexes), often in a highly regulated manner and in a particular temporal sequence." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0008150> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "biological process"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0008150> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "biological_process" .
